WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.134 --> 00:00:13.599
It was the last week in August when Mr.

2
00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:17.681
Irving and Miss Lavender had their wedding in the garden at Miss Lavender's home.

3
00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:23.084
As they said their vows, gentle rays of sunlight shone down upon them.

4
00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:29.048
Paul Irving watched the ceremony happily, looking forward to having a mother once again.

5
00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:31.397
After Mr.

6
00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:36.802
Irving and Miss Lavender had left for their honeymoon and all the wedding guests had gone, Anne stayed

7
00:00:36.842 --> 00:00:38.864
behind to tidy up Miss Lavender's house.

8
00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:43.608
She was staring out the kitchen window when Gilbert came to help her.

9
00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:45.370
"What are you thinking of, Anne?"

10
00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:46.511
Gilbert asked.

11
00:00:46.531 --> 00:00:50.214
"Of Miss Lavender and Mr.

12
00:00:50.394 --> 00:00:52.376
Irving," answered Anne dreamily.

13
00:00:52.396 --> 00:00:59.089
"Isn't it beautiful to think how everything has turned out how they have come together again after all

14
00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:01.691
those years of separation and misunderstanding?"

15
00:01:01.711 --> 00:01:05.833
"Yes, it is beautiful," said Gilbert.

16
00:01:06.694 --> 00:01:08.235
He looked steadily at Anne.

17
00:01:08.255 --> 00:01:14.639
"But wouldn't it have been more beautiful, Anne, if there had been no separation or misunderstanding— if they

18
00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:16.800
had come hand-in-hand all the way through life?"

19
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:23.284
For a moment, Anne's heart fluttered, and for the first time, her eyes faltered under Gilbert's gaze.

20
00:01:24.648 --> 00:01:26.749
It was a strange feeling, and she blushed.

21
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.391
When Anne arrived home, Marilla had some sad news.

22
00:01:31.411 --> 00:01:34.293
"Mr. Lynde has died," she said.

23
00:01:34.313 --> 00:01:37.254
"He died quietly, in his sleep."

24
00:01:38.755 --> 00:01:42.136
Thomas Lynde had been sick for a long time, and Mrs.

25
00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:44.417
Lynde had taken care of him for many years.

26
00:01:45.478 --> 00:01:46.938
Marilla went to comfort Mrs.

27
00:01:46.999 --> 00:01:49.900
Lynde and came back to Green Gables the next morning.

28
00:01:51.964 --> 00:01:58.290
Marilla sat down with Anne, who was eating breakfast, and nervously said, "I suppose Gilbert Blythe is going

29
00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.350
to college in the fall.

30
00:02:00.151 --> 00:02:01.913
Would you like to go to college too?"

31
00:02:02.893 --> 00:02:04.235
Anne looked up, astonished.

32
00:02:04.255 --> 00:02:07.918
"Of course, Marilla, but it's not possible!

33
00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:13.843
I know your eyes are better now, but the twins— they need so much looking after."

34
00:02:13.863 --> 00:02:19.788
"Well, I've always felt that you should go to college," said Marilla.

35
00:02:20.544 --> 00:02:25.906
"You've saved enough from your teaching job for one year at Redmond College, and perhaps you could win

36
00:02:25.946 --> 00:02:28.307
a scholarship to pay for the other years.

37
00:02:29.528 --> 00:02:32.349
Besides, I wouldn't be alone with the twins.

38
00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:34.590
That's what I want to discuss."

39
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.352
Marilla continued, "I had a long talk with Mrs.

40
00:02:39.432 --> 00:02:40.312
Lynde last night.

41
00:02:41.633 --> 00:02:45.294
She has to sell her farm, but she doesn't want to leave Avonlea.

42
00:02:45.854 --> 00:02:49.156
So I suggested she move to Green Gables.

43
00:02:50.048 --> 00:02:51.269
How do you feel about that?"

44
00:02:51.289 --> 00:02:55.331
"Well, that's your decision, Marilla," said Anne.

45
00:02:55.351 --> 00:03:02.615
"Mrs. Lynde is a good woman and a kind neighbor, but "But she's got her faults?"

46
00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.636
Marilla finished, smiling.

47
00:03:04.656 --> 00:03:07.038
"Well, she does, of course.

48
00:03:07.678 --> 00:03:10.800
But if she left Avonlea, I'd miss her terribly.

49
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.182
She's the only close friend I have here.

50
00:03:14.822 --> 00:03:20.857
Mrs. Lynde and I have never had a fight, though we almost did when she met you for

51
00:03:20.897 --> 00:03:21.958
the first time, Anne.

52
00:03:22.818 --> 00:03:23.578
Do you remember?"

53
00:03:23.598 --> 00:03:26.279
"Yes, I do.

54
00:03:26.299 --> 00:03:28.580
I hated her then!"

55
00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:29.601
Anne said.

56
00:03:29.621 --> 00:03:34.663
"Well, you were so different from other children, Anne," said Marilla.

57
00:03:34.683 --> 00:03:37.484
"I didn't know how to manage you at first!

58
00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.565
My brother, Matthew, understood you better."

59
00:03:40.585 --> 00:03:46.388
"Matthew understood everything," said Anne softly, the way she always spoke of him.

60
00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.663
That night Anne thought long and hard about whether to stop teaching and go to college.

61
00:03:53.984 --> 00:04:01.269
She loved every one of her pupils, even the naughty ones, but the idea of college—of learning more—excited

62
00:04:01.329 --> 00:04:03.871
her. The next day Anne resigned.

63
00:04:04.892 --> 00:04:06.052
Meanwhile Mrs.

64
00:04:06.132 --> 00:04:09.855
Lynde gratefully accepted Marilla's offer to move into Green Gables.

65
00:04:11.316 --> 00:04:16.219
Gilbert Blythe was probably the only person who was happy to hear the news that Anne was going

66
00:04:16.259 --> 00:04:16.860
to college.

67
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.682
Her students looked upon it as a catastrophe.

68
00:04:21.463 --> 00:04:23.304
Barbara Shaw cried all night.

69
00:04:23.805 --> 00:04:26.507
Anthony Pye picked a fight because he was so upset.

70
00:04:27.268 --> 00:04:32.372
And Paul Irving defiantly told his father he wouldn't eat any breakfast for a week.

71
00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.074
Diana was sad too.

72
00:04:35.094 --> 00:04:39.217
"It will be horribly lonely here," she moaned.

73
00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:42.760
"You'll have Fred," Anne teased her, giggling.

74
00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.984
"It's all right for you to be happy, Anne," Diana said.

75
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.844
"You're going to college, and you'll have fun and make heaps of lovely new friends."

76
00:04:52.864 --> 00:04:57.468
"I hope I shall make new friends," said Anne thoughtfully.

77
00:04:57.488 --> 00:05:01.431
"New friends make life very interesting.

78
00:05:02.012 --> 00:05:06.455
But no matter how many new friends I make, they'll never be as special to me as the

79
00:05:06.576 --> 00:05:07.076
old ones.

80
00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:11.760
Especially a certain girl with black eyes and dimples.

81
00:05:12.521 --> 00:05:14.182
Can you guess who she is, Diana?"

82
00:05:15.343 --> 00:05:16.304
Diana cheered up.

83
00:05:16.912 --> 00:05:20.755
Anne smiled at her and said, "Do you remember that evening we first met?

84
00:05:21.415 --> 00:05:24.458
We were in your garden and promised eternal friendship.

85
00:05:25.438 --> 00:05:26.879
We've kept that oath, I think.

86
00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.041
I shall never forget that day.

87
00:05:30.762 --> 00:05:35.685
All through my early childhood, nobody cared for me or wanted to be friends with me.

88
00:05:37.407 --> 00:05:40.429
But when I came to Green Gables, everything changed.

89
00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.732
Thank you for your friendship and love, Diana."

90
00:05:46.085 --> 00:05:47.947
Anne and Diana hugged tightly.

91
00:05:49.368 --> 00:05:54.995
No matter where Anne went, they were true friends who would remain in each other's hearts always.
